{"resourceIdentifier":"2745","resourceName":"Wuwei City Afforestation Project in Gansu Province","description":"Wuwei City Afforestation Project in Gansu Province (hereafter referred to as “the project”) is located in Wuwei City, Gansu Province, People’s Republic of China. Wuwei is a prefecture-level city along the Hexi Corridor and the Silk Road where the Loess Plateau, the Tibetan Plateau and the Mongolian Plateau. The project activities involve the planting of trees and shrubs of native species on 28,817.73 hectares (or 432,234 Mu ) of deserts and other barren lands located in Liangzhou District and Gulang County administered by Wuwei City. The species include Picea asperata (Chinese spruce), Platycladus orientalis (Oriental thuja or Oriental arborvitae), Ulmus pumila (Siberian elm), Elaeagnus angustifolia (Russian olive) and Haloxylon ammodendron (saxaul). The project area was barren lands before the project and would continue to be so without the implementation of the project activities. \r\nThe implementation of the project activity will generate GHG emission removals and mitigate climate change, improve soil and water conditions, increase the forest cover and enhance local biodiversity; the project also generates social benefits including job opportunities and technical skills training for local communities and residents.","location":{"latitude":37.500000,"longitude":103.500000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-01-24","endExclusive":"2022-02-24","endInclusive":"2022-02-23"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2745"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Gansu"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"On Hold - see notification letter"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2